                    pretrained on ImageNet, replacing its                       
                    classifier with a single neuron for                         
                    binary classification of malignant vs                       
                    benign/non-neoplastic lesions. We                           
                    apply random horizontal and vertical                        
                    flips, rotations, and normalization to                      
                    train images, with center cropping and                      
                    normalization for validation. We                            
                    perform 5-fold stratified                                   
                    cross-validation, training each fold                        
                    for 3 epochs using Adam and                                 
                    BCEWithLogitsLoss, and compute AUROC                        
