                    performance for distinguishing                              
                    malignant from benign skin lesions. The                     
                    best validation AUROC achieved was                          
                    0.8778, which suggests the model is                         
                    effective for the classification task.                      
                    Validation Metric: 0.8778                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose to address class                          
                    imbalance by using a                                        
                    WeightedRandomSampler in the training                       
                    DataLoader, which will oversample                           
                    malignant cases and ensure each batch                       
                    is balanced. This simple change can                         
                    help the model learn features of the                        
                    minority class more effectively and                         
                    boost the AUROC. The rest of the                            
                    pipeline—including EfficientNet-B0,                         
                    transforms, optimizer, and                                  
                    evaluation—remains unchanged to isolate                     
                    the impact of balanced sampling.                            
