                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose to replace the                            
                    standard BCEWithLogitsLoss with a                           
                    binary focal loss (gamma=2, alpha=0.25)                     
                    to focus training on harder,                                
                    misclassified examples and better                           
                    handle class imbalance. This is an                          
                    atomic change that should improve model                     
                    discrimination without altering the                         
                    rest of the pipeline. We keep                               
                    EfficientNet-B0, augmentations,                             
                    optimizer, and training loop unchanged,                     
                    simply swapping in the focal loss and                       
                    measuring its impact on validation                          
                    AUROC.                                                      
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model showed consistent improvement in                      
                    validation AUROC over 5 epochs,                             
                    reaching a best validation AUROC of                         
                    0.8656. This indicates that the model                       
                    can effectively differentiate malignant                     
                    from benign skin lesions in the dataset                     
                    provided.                                                   
